  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Promotion of Civil and Political Rights in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Victims of human rights abuse and human rights defenders (HRDs), particularly vulnerable and marginalized women, youth and PWDs, have increased access to quality legal, medical, psycho-social, and other support.
 2. Enhanced human rights monitoring, documentation, and information dissemination for evidenced based advocacy.
 3. Women and men, particularly PWDs and youth, are empowered for improved civic participation, holding duty bearers to account and to advocate for reforms.
 4. Civil society partners have increased sustainability and independence to protect and promote human rights.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Promotion of Civil and Political Rights in Zimbabwe. Increasing access to quality legal, medical, psycho-social and other support to victims of human rights abuse and human rights defenders (HRDs)</narrative>
  </description>
